{"id": "849d2ca3-2ecf-4559-b21f-d739db779c70", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check the Bedrock throttle and error metrics, and the runtime's own metrics and logs for the last hour. Then I'll tell you whether anything is failing or being throttled.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_C7ExzAgat8KZlqcDFZbsA3", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "agentcore-model-health", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "searching-logs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether model (Amazon Bedrock) calls made by the Bedrock AgentCore runtime 'llmops_eval_search_agent' are currently failing or being throttled.",
  "context": "User wants a current-status answer (right now). This is a shallow status check, not a root-cause hunt. Report what is observed, with numbers and timestamps; do not speculate on causes.",
  "resources": ["AgentCore runtime name: llmops_eval_search_agent", "Account: 012345678901_1", "Region: us-east-1"],
  "timeframe": "Last 60 minutes ending 2026-11-24T19:05:00Z, compared against the prior 60 minutes as baseline; highlight the last 15 minutes",
  "criteria": "1) Find the runtime (bedrock-agentcore-control list_agent_runtimes / get_agent_runtime) and its CloudWatch log group (typically /aws/bedrock-agentcore/runtimes/<runtime-id>-<endpoint>) and role. 2) Check AgentCore runtime CloudWatch metrics (namespace AWS/Bedrock-AgentCore or similar: invocations, errors, throttles, system/user errors, latency) for the runtime. 3) Check AWS/Bedrock metrics (Invocations, InvocationThrottles, InvocationClientErrors, InvocationServerErrors, InvocationLatency) per ModelId for the models this agent uses (determine from runtime logs/config/env vars; if unknown, check the ModelIds with activity in the window). 4) Run a Logs Insights query on the runtime log group for ThrottlingException, ServiceUnavailable, ModelTimeout, AccessDenied, ValidationException, 429/5xx, 'Too many requests', and count by type per 5 minutes. Return: clear verdict (failing/throttled yes/no), counts and rates vs baseline, exact error messages sampled, which models, and any data you could not access."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check AgentCore runtime and Bedrock model errors and throttling"}], "created_at": null}

